  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a strong downtrend (e.g., Example 2 and 3), the model systematically underestimates volatility and fails to capture sharp mean-reversion spikes, resulting in forecasts that are too low during high-impact events.",
    "The model exhibits a persistent upward bias when sentiment is mixed or slightly positive (0.20) but lacks sufficient downward correction for sudden market reversals seen in the true outcomes.",
    "Forecasts often ignore the 'mean reversion' effect where prices spike after prolonged consolidation, particularly when sentiment history shows low activity followed by a sudden shift.",
    "The model tends to smooth out extreme volatility; corrections should increase forecast variance significantly when the last 5 days of history show a range exceeding 10% of the current price.",
    "In periods of high historical volatility (e.g., Example 4 and 5), the model's linear projection leads to systematic underestimation of peak prices in the first half of the horizon."
  ]
}
